meta {
  name: Reset password
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{ACCOUNTS_API_BASE_URL}}/auth/reset-pwd
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  "newPwd": "Password@02",
  "logoffFromAllSessions": false
}

script:post-response {
  if(res.getStatus() == 200){
      bru.setGlobalEnvVar(
        "MY_PWD", 
        "Password@02"
      );
  }
}

docs {
  This endpoint is used to reset the password. Once the OTP is verified, a one-time use JWT will be generated, allowing the user to reset their password securely.
  
  #### **Steps to Reset Password**
  1. **Call the `Create OTP (ResetPwd)` Endpoint**: This sends an OTP to the user's registered email address for verification.
  
  2. **Call `Verify OTP (ResetPwd)` Endpoint**: Use the OTP received in the email with the `/auth/verify-code` endpoint. Set `requestType` to `"ResetPwd"` in the verification request. Upon successful verification, a one-time JWT is issued.
  
  4. **Call the `Reset Password` Endpoint**: Use the one-time JWT to reset the password securely.
}
